    "drying": {
      "type": "content-columns",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "ink",
        "layout": "boxes",
        "numbered": true,
        "eyebrow": "The other half",
        "heading": "The ride home starts where the ride in finished",
        "lede": "<p>Almost everything in this category is designed around the journey in. A commute has two halves, and only one of them ends near a radiator.</p>",
        "link_label": "How to wash them properly",
        "link_url": "/pages/care-and-washing",
        "mirror": false
      },
      "blocks": {
        "i1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "A shoe won’t dry in eight hours",
            "body": "<p>Especially not under a desk in a building with the heating on a timer. Overshoes protect the shoe on the way in. They don’t dry it by five o’clock.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "A sock can be swapped",
            "body": "<p>A second pair in your bag weighs almost nothing and means the ride home starts dry even if the shoe doesn’t. That’s the practical reason commuters buy two pairs.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Wash cool, air dry overnight",
            "body": "<p>They’ll be ready for the morning. They won’t be ready in two hours, and they must never go on a radiator — direct heat is what finishes a waterproof layer off.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "i1",
        "i2",
        "i3"
      ]
    },
    "fit": {
      "type": "content-columns",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "paper",
        "layout": "cards",
        "numbered": false,
        "eyebrow": "Fit",
        "heading": "Check the shoe before you order",
        "lede": "<p>Cycling shoes have far less room than a walking boot, so this matters more here than anywhere else on the site.</p>",
        "link_label": "The sizes in centimetres",
        "link_url": "/pages/size-guide",
        "mirror": false
      },
      "blocks": {
        "i1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "About the same as a cushioned training sock",
            "body": "<p>If your shoes are already snug in a thin summer sock they’ll be tight in these. Winter and commuting shoes usually have room. Race-fit road shoes often don’t.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Between two sizes, go up",
            "body": "<p>A tight sock in a tight shoe creates a pressure point across your toes that you’ll notice at about mile four.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "If you size up for winter shoes",
            "body": "<p>These fit that space exactly. If you don’t, try them in the shoe before committing to a long ride.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "i1",
        "i2",
        "i3"
      ]
    },
    "problem": {
      "type": "content-columns",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "paper",
        "layout": "steps",
        "numbered": false,
        "eyebrow": "The problem",
        "heading": "Where the water actually comes from",
        "lede": "<p>Riding in the rain isn’t really a rain problem. It’s a spray problem, and spray behaves differently.</p>",
        "mirror": false
      },
      "blocks": {
        "i1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Off the front wheel, onto your ankle",
            "body": "<p>The front wheel throws a constant fan of water backwards onto the shoe and the ankle. That’s where an overshoe stops, and where it’s open.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Standing water, at speed",
            "body": "<p>A puddle taken at twenty miles an hour goes into your shoe through the vents in a way that rain simply doesn’t.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "The road is dirtier than the rain",
            "body": "<p>Road spray carries grit and oil. It stains, it wears things out, and it’s why cycling kit gives up faster than walking kit.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i4": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "And nothing dries at the office",
            "body": "<p>A soaked cycling shoe doesn’t dry under a desk in eight hours. The ride home starts wet whatever the forecast says.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "i1",
